R9 CERTIFIED LEAVE-PAIR-OUT, VERSION 1.0.0

Save this ZIP and its .zip.sha256 sidecar in ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop.
The accompanying command verifies the ZIP, extracts to a new temporary directory,
and runs RUN_R9.command. No copying from Downloads, installation, API request,
Stockfish search, manuscript change, or change to run 2a4e617b40bc occurs.

PROJECT AND EXECUTION
Project: /Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness
Python: /Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/venv/bin/python
Workers: at most 10. Memory budget: 11 GiB. Large fits run alone when necessary.
BLAS threads: one per process. Caffeinate prevents idle sleep.
Private root: derived/replication/r9_certified_v100_PRIVATE/<configuration>/
Desktop pointer: R9_CERTIFIED_LATEST_PRIVATE.json
Aggregate ZIPs and checksums: Desktop/Lichess_Desktop, at 25/50/75/100 percent.
Log: r9_certified_<UTC timestamp>_<pid>.log in the same Desktop folder.
Rerunning the same command resumes authenticated checkpoints and keeps the
originally selected comparison phase. Changed inputs or failed hashes stop.

Runtime planning estimate: 2–5 hours. Allow 4–8 hours if the added comparison
rows require substantial missing ENV history scans. This is not a benchmark.
Progress and ETA messages appear at least every 30 seconds during long stages.
The 25/50/75/100 percentages mark stage completion, not equal fractions of time.
Private caches and temporary numeric arrays can require tens of GB of free disk.
The memory scheduler uses estimates rather than an OS-enforced memory limit.

WHAT IS FROZEN
The vendored IV_Leave_Pair_Out_v1_0_0 package remains byte-for-byte unchanged.
The pinned baseline configuration is:
2a4e617b40bcadacd25887d2035027e4f7777cbe4c2af51b7a7aa7dde592db14
Its complete 14-model report, previously supplied by the user, is authenticated.
Step 0 re-creates S0 and F50 scores from the original donor files, compares every
saved score/count/expected-rate field, and re-estimates all 14 baseline models.
Every available coefficient and standard error, including balance/indicator
rows, is compared to the saved full-precision output. Saved fit tables are also
checked against the authenticated aggregate report. Failure stops R9 estimation.
Numeric tolerance: 2e-10 absolute + 2e-8 relative for coefficients/SEs;
2e-10 absolute for score values. No comparison uses rounded published values.

S0 full: 2,682,329; neutral: 2,452,682. Frozen material flags define neutrality.
The timing-common cohort has the same row hash as the original timing models.
The baseline is held under a shared, read-only lock for the duration of R9.

COMPARISON FRAMES
The default Phase 75 source is the completed analysis configuration
9e46500403a4f3c1c011ec69b5677c295b2d094cca7bddd44f06e5c7ae6b7266:
F75 = 11,057,763; O75 = 7,146,627.
Completed Phase 100 analysis frames take priority on the first launch, even if
that producer's subsequent regression jobs are still pending. Their
configuration, report manifest, completed stage receipts, source/author lineage,
and exact Phase 50 feature bridge must pass. Multiple candidate completed Phase
100 configurations require an explicit --phase-root; the code does not guess.
A downloader's Phase 100 metadata checkpoint without assembled analysis frames
is not a Phase 100 analysis frame. The selected phase is frozen on resume and
reported prominently. The Phase 75 report remains an available-case publication,
with three unresolved selected metadata rows; R9 does not relabel it complete
metadata coverage or manufacture those rows.

Ordinary rows are verified as an exact entry subset. Old Phase 50 features are
checked by game/role/time identity because phase-specific row IDs were rebound.
The entry source intentionally lacks later y/reached columns; those are read
from the certified ordinary frame. ENV definitions stay frozen. Existing
pair/month ENV values are reused; only missing pair/month requests are computed
from authenticated local chronology and existing active-event caches.

SCORES AND CONTROLS
There is one original donor-data scan across 24 monthly partitions, in 16 chooser
shards. It produces the old-score replay and a private reusable event cache.
R9 then reads this cache for A/B/C. O uses the F scores by checked identity.
Ordinary games never become refusals. Author accounts __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__ remain
excluded from both focal roles, donor roles, and the frozen reference model.
The donor chooser is j. All j-to-i decisions are removed at every recorded time;
a reverse-role i-to-j decision cannot enter j-as-chooser history.

A: every eligible recorded donor, before and after, including interval ties.
B: donor event timestamp strictly before focal game START, no 24-hour buffer.
C: donor event timestamp strictly after focal ANCHOR.
B's full-S0 row is never restricted to C-supported rows. Timing comparisons use
the common n_B>=5 and n_C>=5 rows. A's minimum is five throughout. If full-S0 B
has any row below five, the count is exported and the run stops without dropping
or imputing rows. Archived lagged-history support implies this should not occur.

State prediction uses each donor event's own UTC calendar month, including
events that cross a monthly partition boundary. The same two account folds
are excluded as in the baseline. A missing monthly model uses the most recent
usable model no later than that month for the SAME excluded folds. If none
exists, p_hat=0: the donor is retained without a state adjustment. No future
reference model is borrowed for early donors. Terminal-month overflow can use
the final earlier reference. The report lists fallback models, source donor
counts by fold, and affected donor-focal assignments for each frame/variant.
These counts distinguish source donor rows from repeated focal-query uses.

The three A donor-history controls replace their old-cutoff versions in every
model, with the explicitly requested exception that B uses its OWN donor count,
distinct counterpart count, and mean p_hat. C therefore uses A controls under
the stated every-model rule. Its own donor counts/breadth remain available for
diagnostics. This choice is recorded in each result's history_control_donor_set.
The named log-count controls retain the exact
baseline transformations log(1+n) and log(1+distinct counterparts); the change
is their donor set, not a new functional form. Every other control, outcome,
fixed effect and shared-account-OR-date CR0 definition remains fixed.

UNITS AND OUTPUTS
ENV-indicator is primary, with X0 alongside each block. One primary SD is the
root mean squared residual of A in S0 full under ENV-indicator (the residual
mean is absorbed by the fixed effects). All first stages, reduced forms, entry,
placebo and RF contrasts use this SAME SD, plus the exact 0.0594 bridge. The
original baseline's 0.059411690344000595 is used only to reproduce Step 0.
2SLS and its contrasts remain percentage points per receipt. Balance slopes
remain trait SD per the model's native residual-score SD.

A_receipt: A full/neutral, first stage, y/reached reduced forms, 2SLS, Wald and
robust AR 95% intervals, first-stage F and partial R-squared.
B_before_full: B on the identical full S0 rows, with the same outputs.
C_timing: A/B/C on the same supported rows; contrasts contains after-minus-before
RF and 2SLS differences, their cross-equation covariance, SE, intervals and p.
D_placebo: O75/O100 y and reached, 95% and 90% intervals. Contrasts also contains
S0-minus-ordinary RF differences under shared covariance.
E_entry: three frozen entry labels, their base rates and percent of base per SD.
F_balance/F_joint_balance: frozen T30 is SEVEN 30-day traits, not thirty traits.
Holm is within each seven-trait set; the joint test uses stacked trait equations.
G_implied_bias: standardized fifteen traits jointly predict y and received with
FE and X0-NH. Only the trait component forms Y_hat/D_hat. The outer regression
uses the primary controls; X0 is supplied alongside. The full first-order SE
includes fitted prediction-rule uncertainty. These are calibration rows, not
identified causal bias estimates.
H_figure5: twenty equal-count score bins, their mean residual score, mean residual
receipt and conditional CR0 95% intervals, plus the linear first-stage slope.
Ties use stable original row order. Bin membership/score estimation uncertainty
is not propagated in these descriptive intervals.
I_score_diagnostics: donor counts, cross-month and after-anchor shares, fallback
counts, support, and correlations. S0/F50 compare to reproduced archived scores.
For the expanded F frame, the old recipe is recomputed on those same rows; the
added Phase 75/100 rows did not have scores saved by the baseline run.

ADOPTION
If abs(new primary 2SLS - 0.281) > new primary SE / 3, final status is
COMPLETE_ADOPTION_REVIEW_REQUIRED. All tables still finish and export.
The report decomposes the change into donor-month scoring and rebuilt controls,
holding rows fixed. An additional old-score/new-controls fit exposes interactions
and order dependence. This diagnoses numerical movement; it does not decide
whether the revised identifying assumptions are credible. No automatic adoption
or manuscript update occurs, even when the threshold is not exceeded.

OPTIONAL LEARNING SPLITS (ENABLED IN THE SUPPLIED COMMAND)
Two definitions, each with experienced/unexposed groups and both control sets:
full recorded chronology (primary), and the frozen fair_90>0 flag. Full chronology
means an author-clean competitive chooser decision strictly before game start;
it is left-censored at November 2023. The existing 90-day flag retains its frozen
seven-day-buffer window, start-97 days through start-7 days. Group contrasts stack
the two equations under shared covariance. These conditional differences alone
do not establish that kindness was causally 'passed on'.
Use --learning-split none to omit these optional eight fits; the supplied command
uses --learning-split both. With both, 28 R9 fits and 22 contrast rows are planned,
in addition to the fourteen Step 0 model reproductions.

RETURN
R9_CERTIFIED_REPORT_<configuration>_100.zip
R9_CERTIFIED_REPORT_<configuration>_100.zip.sha256
r9_certified_<timestamp>_<pid>.log
The ZIP contains only explicit aggregate tables, diagnostics and certificates.
Scores, account/game identities, raw events and row-level influences stay private.
If stopped, return the latest checkpoint ZIP, its checksum and the log.

OPTIONS
--workers 1..10 --memory-gb 11
--baseline-root /absolute/path/to/2a4e617b40bc
--phase-root /absolute/path/to/a/completed/phase/analysis/configuration
--learning-split both|none
Environment overrides: IV_PROJECT_ROOT, IV_DESKTOP, IV_PYTHON.

VALIDATION LIMIT
Synthetic tests exercise the numerical code, donor logic, data joins, resumed
stages, covariance and export. The private production data are on the research
Mac. Their empirical Step 0 certification and R9 results occur only when the
user runs the package. No new empirical coefficient is claimed in this release.
